# Known issues the image scan (CI, images.yml) skips, each with why and until when, as:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD

# undici 6.29.0, inside npm 12.2.1 (the newest npm, installed in the image): a malicious
# server's answer can crash the program using it. Fixed in undici 6.29.1, which npm doesn't
# bundle yet. kia runs npm only to install esbuild and the guide downloader's packages from
# the npm registry, so the exposure is small. Drop this when a new npm bundles the fix.
CVE-2026-109869 exp:2026-11-30

# Two more in packages npm 12.2.1 bundles (npm's newest, which still ships them). Checked in
# kia's image, 2026-10-26; drop each when a new npm bundles the fix.
# undici 6.29.0: a server's EventSource stream can use up memory (fixed in 6.29.1). In npm,
# only node-gyp's downloader loads undici. node-gyp runs only from install scripts, and kia
# installs with --ignore-scripts (kia.grab); nothing else in npm uses EventSource.
CVE-2026-109924 exp:2026-11-30
# ip-address 10.7.2: an IPv6 address full of percent signs takes long to parse (fixed in
# 10.7.4). In npm, only its SOCKS proxy support (socks) uses it, and kia sets no SOCKS proxy.
CVE-2026-111997 exp:2026-11-30
